Taking from SamR's [answer](https://stackoverflow.com/a/77437696/3720258):

`y1[i]` and `y2[i]` are elements of writable integer vectors, and are of type cpp11::writable::r_vector<int>::proxy. It appears that the equals operator for this type has been defined in two places:

